\section{Frozen hypothesis and isolated change}
\textbf{Hypothesis.} \VAR{summary.hypothesis|latex}

The prior direct shortcut is additive:
\[
\delta_{\mathrm{old}}=w^\top[h;x]+b.
\]
It cannot change its history coefficients with forecast lead. The tested
shortcut adds only a low-rank multiplicative interaction:
\[
\delta_{\mathrm{new}}=w^\top[h;x]+b+
v^\top\{\tanh(Ax)\odot\tanh(Bh)\}.
\]
Here \(x\) is the 126-value multiscale history vector and \(h\) is the
192-wide Fourier horizon embedding. The additive output and interaction
output were initialized to zero, preserving the persistence anchor.

