\section{Claim boundary, limitations, and next action}
This single-fold, single-seed screen cannot establish seasonal robustness,
instrument transfer, operational readiness, or a champion. Low-rank
factorization also constrains the possible lead-specific coefficient changes,
while the shared deep branch and probability head still co-adapt during
training. The result therefore rejects only the three frozen ranks under this
training budget; it does not show that horizon conditioning is universally
unhelpful.

The evidence does show that the remaining Fusion v2.5 gap was not repaired by
this direct multiplicative shortcut. Together with the closed tail-loss and
residual-cap cycles, the responsible next step is program synthesis, not an
unregistered fourth rank or a post-metric architecture tweak.

